sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch12-16> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch12-16--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch12-16--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on wolfram2002-ch12-16: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.53" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.528"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    dct:type "resolution-route/mixed" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.64"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Cook's proof that rule 110 is universal, together with the emulation argument, settles the claim for that constructed system. The sentence also covers many common systems and almost any behavior that seems complex. One universality proof leaves that wider scope open, and a picture that resembles a cellular automaton is not a test of a natural system." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: For a universal system such as rule 110, check a published emulation proof that any uniform predictor can itself be emulated, so nothing systematically outruns the system. Listing common natural systems and asking whether each has a closed form is a separate test, and only the first is available now." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Common and seems complex are observer-relative.", "Universality blocks a uniform shortcut for every input, while a single input may still have a shortcut.", "Looking like a simple program is weak evidence that a natural system is universal." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/wolfram2002-ch12-16--grok--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/wolfram2002-ch12-16--grok--dataset-2> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch12-16--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of wolfram2002-ch12-16 by Grok 4.7: 0.45" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.45"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch12-16--grok> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch12-16> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch12-16--grok--operationalizability> .
